*> The work state of one chunk being generated by steps (core/src/gen-job.cob; research R12): included at level 05 under a
*> group. A job is started (GEN-JOB-START), advanced one step at a time (GEN-JOB-STEP, which does the work of the stage
*> GJ-STAGE at step GJ-SUB of it) and complete when GJ-STAGE is past the last stage; the chunk memory is the job's own
*> until the chunk is installed. The same steps run back to back are the atomic reference (GEN-JOB-RUN-ALL).
*> The generation queue holds one such job (GENQUEUE.cpy GQ-JOB); an atomic generation holds its own.
    05 GJ-ACTIVE            BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-DIM               BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-CX                BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-CZ                BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-STAGE             BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-SUB               BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-STEPS             BINARY-LONG.
    05 GJ-ADDR              USAGE POINTER.
    05 GJ-FINAL-ROOT        BINARY-LONG.
*>  heightmaps: the y of the highest recorded block, -65 for an empty column; index z * 16 + x + 1
    05 GJ-HEIGHTS.
       10 GJ-HM-SURFACE     BINARY-LONG OCCURS 256 TIMES.
       10 GJ-HM-OCEAN       BINARY-LONG OCCURS 256 TIMES.
    05 GJ-GRID.
       COPY GENGRID.
